%n ana [... | na]mirti? (|) ilī || illakū | supûʾa
#note: See @bib{RN117@862}: “The trace after @i{a-na} is not certainly @akk{DI[NGIR]}, either here or in the apparent parallel l. 25, but the indirect object of @i{illikū suppûʾa} is very likely a deity. The plural imperative @i{šullimāʾinni} in l. 12 presupposes that more than one deity was invoked, and thus rules out a repetition of  @akk{{d}}@i{sîn} from l. 10. As the most prominent of the astral deities, Venus is perhaps the foremost candidate for restoration here, but this is uncertain while the trace before @i{šullimāʾinni} in l. 12 is undeciphered. (…) If it is right to restore a divine name following @i{ana}, there is not room enough in the break also to accommodate the standard epithet @i{šākin}(@i{at}) @i{namirti} (used of both Sîn and Šamaš, and also the fire god: see @i{CAD} N/1, p. 229). As a provisional solution I propose simply DN @i{namirti}.”
// cf. L I.4 SB "IX" 25

